==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequiredEverywhere  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequiredEverywhere.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuthRequiredEverywhere allows Alloy to construct an EditOperation, DeleteOperation, or CreateOperation with no caller (unauthenticated). The injected violation forces such a callerless DeleteOperation to exist, which the AuthRequiredEverywhere and FR_001_AuthRequired assertions should catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog allows two distinct DeleteOperations to share the same TaskDeletion log entry, violating the one-entry-per-deletion invariant. The injected violation forces two DeleteOperations to share a log entry.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_018_DeletionLogged
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Removing F_AttributionCorrectness lets a CreateOperation produce a Task whose creator is a different Member than the operation's authenticated caller. The injection forces this mismatch, directly violating FR-002 and FR-009.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_IdentityFromAuthContext, FR_009_CreatorRecordedImmutable
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_IdentityFromAuthContext: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_CreatorRecordedImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskEditRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskEditRule.als
    rationale: Removing F_ClosedTaskEditRule allows an EditOperation targeting a Done task to carry no newStatus (or to set newStatus = Done), representing an illegal in-place edit of a closed task. The injection forces such an operation to exist.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionLogged  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionLogged.als
    rationale: Removing F_DeletionLogged allows a DeleteOperation whose logEntry.deletedBy differs from its caller, breaking the attribution invariant in the deletion audit trail. The injection forces this misattribution.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_018_DeletionLogged
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_InitialStatusTodo  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_InitialStatusTodo.als
    rationale: Removing F_InitialStatusTodo allows a CreateOperation to produce a Task whose initial status is InProgress or Done rather than Todo. The injection forces a newly produced Task to have status Done.
    expected to FAIL: FR_010_InitialStatusTodo
      - FR_010_InitialStatusTodo: FAIL (expected)

